homeproxy (MiWiFi / iptables port)
=================================

A sing-box front-end for routers without LuCI, ucode, or nftables (e.g. stock
Xiaomi/MiWiFi). The original luci-app-homeproxy (LuCI JS + ucode + fw4/nftables)
is replaced by:

  * Lua backend (on-device `lua 5.1` + `luci.json` + `uci` binding)
  * iptables + ipset traffic steering (TCP redirect / UDP tproxy / DNS hijack)
  * a shell CLI (`homeproxy ...`) instead of a web UI

Quick start (on the router, after deploying the files under /):

  homeproxy add "My SS" -- shadowsocks 1.2.3.4 8388 password=secret \
      shadowsocks_encrypt_method=aes-256-gcm
  homeproxy main-node <section>          # use `homeproxy nodes` to find it
  homeproxy routing-mode bypass_mainland_china
  homeproxy proxy-mode redirect_tproxy
  homeproxy lan-proxy global             # or listed_only / except_listed
  homeproxy generate
  homeproxy restart
  homeproxy log -f

Subscription update and resource refresh:

  homeproxy subscribe
  homeproxy update-resources all

Notes
-----
  * sing-box is not bundled; install a compatible `sing-box` binary and point
    `HP_SINGBOX` at it (default `/usr/bin/sing-box`).
  * On MiWiFi the root filesystem is read-only — place the files on a writable
    layer (e.g. /data with symlinks, or rebuild the firmware) and keep
    `/etc/config/homeproxy` on the persistent config partition.
  * Only TCP redirect + UDP tproxy (+ DNS hijack) modes are wired for iptables;
    the `tun` mode requires the tun kmod and is best-effort.

